(6618428, 987300, 141542, '<td valign="top">Giles_uk,<br/> <br/>I didn''t feel your photo was abrasive or edgy really.  I understood what you meant by freedom for the condemned, and that''s all very clear.  This is a well lit noose to me, and that''s about it.  If you look at the top shot, for example, that''s an image that conveys emotion, and a very special moment that fits the subject perfectly, and it just happens to be a dog.  People may say "Well, people like dog shots because they''re cute."  I would beg to disagree, and I think you''d disagree too.  People hate dog shots, because they represent a few things:<br/> <br/>1) Amateur hour<br/>2) People who aren''t adventurous with photography<br/>3) More of the same<br/> <br/>However, it requires a unique shot to be something special in my eyes, and I just don''t feel like you captured something unique.<br/> <br/>If you had shot a man injecting heroin, head titled back, eyes closed, and the light falling on his face, or even simulated this (slightly strange), now that would''ve earned a 10 from me.<br/> <br/>Just my opinion, and that is something that is just as subjective as anyone else here.<br/> <br/>Looking back, I think this shot deserved a 6 or 7 from me, and I regret the 5.</td>', 'Giles_uk, I didn''t feel your photo was abrasive or edgy really.  I understood what you meant by freedom for the condemned, and that''s all very clear.  This is a well lit noose to me, and that''s about it.  If you look at the top shot, for example, that''s an image that conveys emotion, and a very special moment that fits the subject perfectly, and it just happens to be a dog.  People may say "Well, people like dog shots because they''re cute."  I would beg to disagree, and I think you''d disagree too.  People hate dog shots, because they represent a few things: 1) Amateur hour2) People who aren''t adventurous with photography3) More of the same However, it requires a unique shot to be something special in my eyes, and I just don''t feel like you captured something unique. If you had shot a man injecting heroin, head titled back, eyes closed, and the light falling on his face, or even simulated this (slightly strange), now that would''ve earned a 10 from me. Just my opinion, and that is something that is just as subjective as anyone else here. Looking back, I think this shot deserved a 6 or 7 from me, and I regret the 5.', '2011-12-14 16:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6618433, 987366, 141542, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jagar:</b></div><hr/><i> Don''t understand this place, thought this would surely be near the top. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Same here, disappointed to see where this ended up.  I''ll say no more...but let your imagination take care of that! :/</td>', 'Originally posted by jagar: Don''t understand this place, thought this would surely be near the top.   Same here, disappointed to see where this ended up.  I''ll say no more...but let your imagination take care of that! :/', '2011-12-14 17:03:58.000000', NULL, 0),
