(6619943, 986897, 68947, '<td valign="top">Jo, I''m so sorry that there''s a couple of self-proclaimed "know-it-alls" in here, disrupting your enjoyment of having just won this ribbon.  Perhaps, they do need some help in learning etiquette.  (A statement, not a question).<br/> <br/>Dudski and Kgeary...neither of you have any idea of what it is that you''re talking about.  There have been PLENTY of photos gracing the front pages of this site that I have had to head scratch, wondering why they are there.  However, they are there.  Enough people found merit and beauty in the shot to put it there.  The same holds true with this one.  Accept it...your particular tastes or not.  <br/> <br/>As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.  <br/> <br/>Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated.<br/> <br/>Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one.</td>', 'Jo, I''m so sorry that there''s a couple of self-proclaimed "know-it-alls" in here, disrupting your enjoyment of having just won this ribbon.  Perhaps, they do need some help in learning etiquette.  (A statement, not a question). Dudski and Kgeary...neither of you have any idea of what it is that you''re talking about.  There have been PLENTY of photos gracing the front pages of this site that I have had to head scratch, wondering why they are there.  However, they are there.  Enough people found merit and beauty in the shot to put it there.  The same holds true with this one.  Accept it...your particular tastes or not.   As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.   Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated. Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one.', '2011-12-16 21:06:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6620023, 986712, 54645, '<td valign="top">Regarding your question about impact and my initial comment.  Keep in mind, this is one opinion. . . as it stands, it is very appealing. I can see it in a tutorial or a written piece on free running. For a greater human impact, it needs context. . . other participants, or random people, watching. . . I can imagine the varied expressions as they watched. It becomes a street image, or candid, loaded with story, not the least of which is the act of free running in a rigid city environment, etc. That would make it memorable beyond the splendid action. Cheers, Ben<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-12-17 00:01:22.</i></td>', 'Regarding your question about impact and my initial comment.  Keep in mind, this is one opinion. . . as it stands, it is very appealing. I can see it in a tutorial or a written piece on free running. For a greater human impact, it needs context. . . other participants, or random people, watching. . . I can imagine the varied expressions as they watched. It becomes a street image, or candid, loaded with story, not the least of which is the act of free running in a rigid city environment, etc. That would make it memorable beyond the splendid action. Cheers, Ben', '2011-12-16 23:57:02.000000', '2011-12-17 00:01:22.000000', 0),
