(6620171, 986897, 141542, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by J-Me:</b></div><hr/><i> Jo, I''m so sorry that there''s a couple of self-proclaimed "know-it-alls" in here, disrupting your enjoyment of having just won this ribbon.  Perhaps, they do need some help in learning etiquette.  (A statement, not a question).<br/> <br/>Dudski and Kgeary...neither of you have any idea of what it is that you''re talking about.  There have been PLENTY of photos gracing the front pages of this site that I have had to head scratch, wondering why they are there.  However, they are there.  Enough people found merit and beauty in the shot to put it there.  The same holds true with this one.  Accept it...your particular tastes or not.  <br/> <br/>As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.  <br/> <br/>Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated.<br/> <br/>Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>While I agree with you about not bashing people, that''s just not true for the photographic world as a whole.  I''ve been told many times by my brother-in-law, a highly qualified, professional wedding photographer that there are many times a photo coach of his would literally say "WTF were you thinking here?"  Sometimes that gets the point across, sometimes it doesn''t.<br/> <br/>Regardless of all that, there is some pretty clear and unusual editing near the bottom center of this image. You can see a very clear line seperating two parts of the image on the right side.  Now, I am new here, but when I read the Basic Editing rules with these virgin eyes of mine, I see a problem with this image being valid.  That is all there is to it.  I think it''s a good concept as a shot, and I think there are some redeeming qualities about it, but I don''t believe it''s a valid submission.</td>', 'Originally posted by J-Me: Jo, I''m so sorry that there''s a couple of self-proclaimed "know-it-alls" in here, disrupting your enjoyment of having just won this ribbon.  Perhaps, they do need some help in learning etiquette.  (A statement, not a question). Dudski and Kgeary...neither of you have any idea of what it is that you''re talking about.  There have been PLENTY of photos gracing the front pages of this site that I have had to head scratch, wondering why they are there.  However, they are there.  Enough people found merit and beauty in the shot to put it there.  The same holds true with this one.  Accept it...your particular tastes or not.   As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.   Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated. Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one.   While I agree with you about not bashing people, that''s just not true for the photographic world as a whole.  I''ve been told many times by my brother-in-law, a highly qualified, professional wedding photographer that there are many times a photo coach of his would literally say "WTF were you thinking here?"  Sometimes that gets the point across, sometimes it doesn''t. Regardless of all that, there is some pretty clear and unusual editing near the bottom center of this image. You can see a very clear line seperating two parts of the image on the right side.  Now, I am new here, but when I read the Basic Editing rules with these virgin eyes of mine, I see a problem with this image being valid.  That is all there is to it.  I think it''s a good concept as a shot, and I think there are some redeeming qualities about it, but I don''t believe it''s a valid submission.', '2011-12-17 09:54:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6620502, 986897, 118503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by J-Me:</b></div><hr/><i> Jo, I''m so sorry that there''s a couple of self-proclaimed "know-it-alls" in here, disrupting your enjoyment of having just won this ribbon.  Perhaps, they do need some help in learning etiquette.  (A statement, not a question).<br/> <br/>Dudski and Kgeary...neither of you have any idea of what it is that you''re talking about.  There have been PLENTY of photos gracing the front pages of this site that I have had to head scratch, wondering why they are there.  However, they are there.  Enough people found merit and beauty in the shot to put it there.  The same holds true with this one.  Accept it...your particular tastes or not.  <br/> <br/>As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.  <br/> <br/>Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated.<br/> <br/>Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>And if it''s shown to be not valid, I''ll accept your apology.</td>', 'Originally posted by J-Me: Jo, I''m so sorry that there''s a couple of self-proclaimed "know-it-alls" in here, disrupting your enjoyment of having just won this ribbon.  Perhaps, they do need some help in learning etiquette.  (A statement, not a question). Dudski and Kgeary...neither of you have any idea of what it is that you''re talking about.  There have been PLENTY of photos gracing the front pages of this site that I have had to head scratch, wondering why they are there.  However, they are there.  Enough people found merit and beauty in the shot to put it there.  The same holds true with this one.  Accept it...your particular tastes or not.   As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.   Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated. Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one.   And if it''s shown to be not valid, I''ll accept your apology.', '2011-12-17 21:53:41.000000', NULL, 0),
