(6621614, 986897, 21304, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by J-Me:</b></div><hr/><i> As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms of editing techniques.  Just because YOU can''t figure out how they''re done "legally" doesn''t mean that they ARE illegal.  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agreed. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by J-Me:</b></div><hr/><i> Too bad neither one of you could censor yourselves enough to either not comment if you had nothing good to say about a winning entry...or...simply refrained from commenting (as I do when I don''t agree with a ribboner) and waited to see if it was validated.<br/> <br/>Both of you will look like fools when this ribbon sticks.  I hope your photos receive the same curteousness as what you''ve shown here on this one. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>please re-read my post and you''ll see that I 1) offered congratulations, 2) claimed that I didn''t believe that the entry was legal, and 3) was convinced that it wasn''t legal and said that something doesn''t look quite right (i.e. fishy)... ummm. that''s about it. no personal attacks on the photographer, no saying "holy crap I have no clue how this photo won... , etc."<br/> <br/>..and since when do all comments on winning entries need to be positive? And all this talk of needing help, apologies, sarcastic remarks, and looking like a fool?? now THOSE are personal attacks.. this place is getting whack.<br/> <br/>Upon further reflection, I now realize this is why I don''t comment on many photos around here you say something that''s perceived as being even slightly out of line and people trip balls and start firing off negative messages left right and center. Anyhow, have a good day all.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-12-19 10:34:49.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by J-Me: As for looking "fishy"...there are all kinds of forms 